DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseemm__ppoosstt() function increments (unlocks) the semaphore pointed to by
     _s_e_m.  If there are threads blocked on the semaphore when sseemm__ppoosstt() is
     called, then the highest priority thread that has been blocked the long‐
     est on the semaphore will be allowed to return from sseemm__wwaaiitt().

     The sseemm__ppoosstt() function is signal-reentrant and may be called within sig‐
     nal handlers.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The sseemm__ppoosstt() function returns the value 0 if successful; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The sseemm__ppoosstt() function will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The _s_e_m argument points to an invalid semaphore.

     [EOVERFLOW]        The semaphore value would exceed SEM_VALUE_MAX.

